Why TX polling is combined with RX polling

Key insight:

RX and TX both require reading NIC state
Both involve DMA rings
Both benefit from batching

So Linux combines them:

One polling loop (NAPI)

One softirq (NET_RX_SOFTIRQ)

Both RX + TX handled together

This prevents:

RX starvation due to TX floods

TX starvation due to RX floods
